<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Shandong Lashes Out, 2021</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Shandong Lashes Out, 2021&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al "Beirutdude" Sandrik&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;The Time Is: 14 August, 2021, 11:00 Zulu/14 August 2021, 18:00 Cam Ranh Bay Time&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Cam Ranh Bay, Vietnam&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playable as&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;STRONG&gt;PLAN Only&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Duration:&amp;nbsp;1 day 12 hours&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Built under C:MO v1.02 – Build 1147.23&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Database: DB3000 v488&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Background: &lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;On July 31st a Vietnam People’s Navy (VPN) supply vessel on a resupply mission to Amboyna Cay, Spratley Islands was deliberately shouldered (rammed side-to-side) by a large PRC Coast Guard vessel. Two days later she returned with the VPN Gepard Class Frigate &lt;A name=_Hlk71913681&gt;&lt;I&gt;Đinh Tiên Hoàng&lt;/I&gt; &lt;/A&gt;(HQ-011) acting as escort. Upon arrival the VPN vessels confronted the PRC Coast Guard vessel blocking access to the pier area. After some frantic maneuvering the&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;Zhaotou class cutter &lt;I&gt;Haijing 2901&lt;/I&gt; shouldered the Vietnamese frigate causing some damage. In the excitement the gun crew of the &lt;I&gt;Đinh Tiên Hoàng&lt;/I&gt;‘s 76.2 mm/59-caliber AK–176 gun engaged the Chinese vessel raking the Bridge and killing 12 members of the crew including the both Ship’s Captain and Political Officer.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;The engagement only took a few seconds but the damage was done. The Vietnamese vessels quickly retired making their best speed for their home port of Cam Ranh Bay. That evening they were found and engaged by four Su-30MKK fighter jets from Subi Reef dropping KAB-500L laser-guided bombs. &lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;Five bombs hit the supply vessel leaving it a burning hulk and two near misses caused severe damage to systems on the Gepard. After picking up survivors from the supply vessel the &lt;I&gt;Đinh Tiên Hoàng &lt;/I&gt;returned at best speed to Cam Ranh Bay for repairs. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;Tensions spiked between the PRC and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam. Accusations were traded in the U.N., Media and, most importantly, between both sides’ military commanders. PLA forces began a build up along the Vietnamese border drawing in Vietnamese reinforcements. Western analysts were on TV and radio hyping a repeat of the 1979 The Sino-Vietnamese War but the PRC leadership had no intention of crossing the border, the buildup was just a diversion. In fact, the PRC Central Military Commission determined a message must be sent to all of the counties disputing their South China Seas/Nine-Dash Line claims, the carrier Shandong, supported by H-6Ks would destroy the &lt;I&gt;Đinh Tiên Hoàng&lt;/I&gt; and other vessels/facilities at Cam Ran Bay.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;Saturday evening, August 14th, the Shandong Carrier Strike Group (CSG) departed Yulin Naval Base and turned west toward Haiphong harbor. This too was a ruse, after sunset and just outside the shipping lanes (Sceanrio starting position) the CSG turned south and began a high-speed run toward Cam Ranh Bay. Meanwhile H-6Ks at Leiyang Air Base were readied with cruise missiles to support the attack. A Ming Class SSK and Type-093G SSN have also been assigned to support your attack and are taking up positions near Cam Ranh Bay.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Mission:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt; Your mission is to destroy VPN vessels and facilities at Cam Ranh Bay while avoiding losses to your assets.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Notes: &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;Many units (including your submarines) teleport, please run the scenario for five (5) seconds before setting any missions. You should then delete the HIGHLIGHTED “&lt;STRONG&gt;Teleport&lt;/STRONG&gt;” Reference points after teleporting has completed.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;To balance the scenario the H-6Ks are in "reserve" (for 24 hours). Choose your load outs&amp;nbsp;for them right away but they won't be available until the next day. So in other words, you load out your aircraft but instead of them being available in 20 hours it will take 24 hours to load them.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;The J-15s on the Shandong, are also in "reserve" and you also choose their loadouts. They&amp;nbsp;will be available in the normal 10 hours as you move the Shandon CSG into position to launch. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;I did set ASW/AEW missions for the Shandong CSG, delete/adjust them&amp;nbsp;as you see fit. At a minimum these missions would be underway as the carrier leaves port. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;The merchant shipping/shipping lanes are based on Marine AIS Tracking and represent a MERE FRACTION of what is really out there at any given time. You have MPA/UAV assets on Hainan Island to monitor them.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Sides begin “Neutral” but will change posture as PLAN/PLAAF units cross into Vietnamese Exclusion Zones. This just keeps the A/I from firing prematurely.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;For the first&amp;nbsp;12 hours your KJ-2000 AEW aircraft (should) automatically launch to maintain patrol coverage&amp;nbsp;in the AEW mission area off Cam Ranh Bay. After that you will have to launch them to maintain patrol operations without interpution.&amp;nbsp;Again adjust this as you see fit, just trying to make mission designation easier as this one is a pretty standard mission.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Scoring: &lt;/STRONG&gt;0 points = Disaster and 12,000 a Triumph. Your targets are the ships and Naval Base. You don’t recieve any points for attacking airports.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Built under C:MO v1.02 Build 1147.23 Database: DB3000 v488&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;A &lt;STRONG&gt;Delta File is provided for deep rebuilds.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al "BeirutDude" Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
